It replaces the earlier services/model-training code. It does not use, import,
bundle or depend on unsloth or unsloth_zoo (AGPL-3.0); tools/spdx_gate.py fails
the build if either is imported or listed as a dependency.

At run time it uses these separately installed libraries, each under its own
license (none is bundled in this folder):
  torch          BSD-3-Clause (PyTorch; bundles third-party code under
                 Apache-2.0, MIT, BSL-1.0, ISC, Zlib per its package metadata)
  transformers   Apache-2.0
  peft           Apache-2.0
  trl            Apache-2.0
  accelerate     Apache-2.0
  datasets       Apache-2.0
  safetensors    Apache-2.0
  huggingface_hub Apache-2.0
  bitsandbytes   MIT (QLoRA only)

GGUF export runs llama.cpp's convert_hf_to_gguf.py and llama-quantize (MIT)
as separate programs when they are already on the computer. They are not
bundled or downloaded by allternit-tune.
